arginal hand that cannot withstand a raise. Since I am in position and the opponent checked, checking back allows me to see the river for free, realizing my equity and potentially improving to a straight or two pair without risking more chips unnecessarily.\n\nReason: Checking is the prudent play to control the pot size with a marginal hand (3rd pair) while retaining the chance to hit a straight on the river or win at showdown against missed high cards.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
